#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078208 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "98fdea06-a5ad-5d22-b928-ef893424e447" :question/math-academy-id "e-158" :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $1.1$ | $1.3$ | $1.7$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate $f'(x)$ at the point $x=0.2$ using a central difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=0.2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0.2) & ≈\\frac{f(0.2+0.1)-f(0.2-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0.3)-f(0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.7-1.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.6}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078209 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078607 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "62934fda-d972-50d5-acdb-e1f7b2fd63f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-159" :question/problem "![](images/53/5355859a0307e46ae84d12bc5e0b183d72458972c8a417fb6d9296b4769ea078.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{g(x+h) - g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+4)-g(4-4)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(8)-g(0)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-(-10)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078212 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078608 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "d405fda1-1111-56db-ae34-4c0f257852f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-160" :question/problem "A car engine is being heated from a temperature of about $-10^{\\circ}.$ The temperature of the engine after $t$ minutes is given by $T(t).$  The graph of $T(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/fe/fe78a78911e2df9cdb488ec57b0e0a34bb56e18b57303d895dc8013b64a4afc3.png)\n\nApproximate the rate at which the temperature of the engine increases when $t = 3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nT'(t) \\approx \\dfrac{T(t+h) - T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{T(3+1)-T(3-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(4)-T(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{60-30}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of temperature increase is approximately $15^{\\circ}$ per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "167457a9-b6b4-5440-b129-2f0689b6e02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281898} {:answer/id #uuid "2f6ae62d-82cc-507a-a390-da0ec1363bb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282109} {:answer/id #uuid "30d44fd4-c8bf-5a7d-8db2-4407697e9981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282125} {:answer/id #uuid "534f1b55-dd7e-54a5-b639-76254d4ef738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282400} {:answer/id #uuid "b830ca2d-56fe-5d6d-b7b4-790849ecdebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "534f1b55-dd7e-54a5-b639-76254d4ef738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282400} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f3db73c-bd8b-5985-8c46-305bfc25d447" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a448f94c-9203-5aa7-907f-0bb1a9165bbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-170649" :question/problem "Given that $f(2.9)=5.91$ and $f(3.1)=7.11,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(3).$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+0.1)-f(3-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3.1)-f(2.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7.11-5.91}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.2}{0.2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508103 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ccbeb88-908d-55b3-a125-61b3f46ff08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ccbeb88-908d-55b3-a125-61b3f46ff08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507617} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bea8aec-8ac7-571d-93ce-c41382fa0763" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62032b2-c1a5-5a5d-886c-e5b808c77233" :question/math-academy-id "q-314288" :question/problem "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $0.6$ | $0.8$ | $1$ | $1.2$ | $1.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $2.6$ | $1.9$ | $1.5$ | $2.3$ | $5.9$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0.8$ using a central difference approximation.\n\n${g}^{′}(0.8)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=0.8.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(0.8) & ≈\\frac{g(0.8+0.2)-g(0.8-0.2)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(1)-g(0.6)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5-2.6}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.1}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-11}{4} \\\\  & =-2.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c4547a7-1728-5d73-a024-93e088d07cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c4547a7-1728-5d73-a024-93e088d07cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507688} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea39bfa2-a209-51aa-80a0-fff9f13a2672" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02a39903-e9f1-5373-88d1-5e7a858c1c6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-314885" :question/problem "Given that $f(1.9)=4.21$ and $f(2.1)=5.81,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(2).$\n\n${f}^{′}(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=2$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{f(2+0.1)-f(2-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2.1)-f(1.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5.81-4.21}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.6}{0.2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078607 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7e2085a-e531-5baf-8fe5-1d1d7a6ad9e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7e2085a-e531-5baf-8fe5-1d1d7a6ad9e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296148} :answer-field/id #uuid "8369a49e-b4e6-517f-b327-76c2f9620e9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4894e4a4-bc69-5cbe-8eef-c136c4c17945" :question/math-academy-id "q-314898" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d27b0d70171683240fd44c8bbbcc8cb46ce0f0f216533a8061d31a991cce4e14.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=1$ and $x=3.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=2$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{f(2+1)-f(2-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3)-f(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)}{2} \\\\  & =-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3098c1b5-fa3f-59d6-b4d0-17b2888a2595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3098c1b5-fa3f-59d6-b4d0-17b2888a2595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507665} :answer-field/id #uuid "83cf222e-a725-5f50-9a9c-5106f3f53afc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0089d6b7-bea1-5c5c-b759-cd65107e82f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-343983" :question/problem "Given that $f(1.25)=0.75$ and $f(1.75)=-0.50,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(1.5).$\n\n${f}^{′}(1.5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=1.5$ with the step size $h=0.25.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(1.5) & ≈\\frac{f(1.5+0.25)-f(1.5-0.25)}{2(0.25)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1.75)-f(1.25)}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-0.50-0.75}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1.25)}{0.5} \\\\  & =-2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078607 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbd1d74-f9fa-51ba-8016-e774785e51b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbd1d74-f9fa-51ba-8016-e774785e51b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507756} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f57be83-0954-54b9-b4ea-a48c439af8b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a10d42c-0c01-597c-81cf-42c95eadf6ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-344003" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e526d91e13619efd7dfd8cab4143a43a4e0d373ad2766a0aac2de02a8f7ec7f8.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-2$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=2.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=-4$ and $x=0.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(-2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-2$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-2) & ≈\\frac{f(-2+2)-f(-2-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0)-f(-4)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078607 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bba96510-3aad-52e6-933c-3020fe0f7265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bba96510-3aad-52e6-933c-3020fe0f7265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316180} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7d58ba-9fa1-5287-b687-96086e2fe893" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe82b330-59ab-5f93-9994-eddddff07551" :question/math-academy-id "q-344023" :question/problem "![](images/56/5663e7c59a9f42b31ebadd9abb54e36c604526c00334f840014a674c5b6dcdb8.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=6$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=3.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=3$ and $x=9.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(6)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=6$ with step size $h=3.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{f(6+3)-f(6-3)}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(9)-f(3)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)}{6} \\\\  & =-0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508086 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078607 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd90a7dc-ed12-541e-9465-1c706693c184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd90a7dc-ed12-541e-9465-1c706693c184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507896} :answer-field/id #uuid "45759e68-39d9-53a8-920d-06189f95b4ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9bc69072-1729-5358-9591-a855b171ce26" :question/math-academy-id "q-344026" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c2d36807b25464536f395912dad0443831f4846f23a337e9495cf673bd488d6.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=1$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=0$ and $x=2.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=1$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{f(1+1)-f(1-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2)-f(0)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-(-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078608 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bed2ee92-7821-5be1-89a3-320104da1adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bed2ee92-7821-5be1-89a3-320104da1adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507861} :answer-field/id #uuid "369cc8e3-5474-53d6-a060-3bb5cec64cd1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bf64a24-1ed0-5d2f-8ee9-666d256fd892" :question/math-academy-id "q-344364" :question/problem "In a nutrition study, the mass of bacteria in a culture (in $\\text{g}$) after $t$ hours is given by the function $M(t).$ The values of $M(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1.5$ | $1.8$ | $2.1$ | $2.4$ | $2.7$ | $3.0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$M(t)$** | $6.2$ | $6.8$ | $7.5$ | $8.1$ | $8.7$ | $9.3$ |\n\nApproximate the bacteria’s mass instantaneous rate of change at $t=2.4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.3.$\n\nThe bacteria’s mass at $t=2.4$ is changing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $g$ per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{M(t+h)-M(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=2.4$ with step size $h=0.3.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{′}(2.4) & ≈\\frac{M(2.4+0.3)-M(2.4-0.3)}{2(0.3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{M(2.7)-M(2.1)}{0.6} \\\\  & =\\frac{8.7-7.5}{0.6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.2}{0.6} \\\\  & =2.0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the bacteria’s mass at $t=2.4$ is changing at approximately $2.0\\,g$ per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508066 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078608 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b1993e-1478-5444-9608-5ffec37aa265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507610} {:answer/id #uuid "4641b589-d1df-5109-886b-057522bb0ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507707} {:answer/id #uuid "7370b0a8-d27a-5f48-973e-074b1f8d6139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507767} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0cb2fe-db1d-5364-896a-42e989e126d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507797} {:answer/id #uuid "e509c827-a594-508a-9b0a-727051003b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7370b0a8-d27a-5f48-973e-074b1f8d6139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507767} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab13eb1-4f8f-5f20-84da-006bd8395175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "630319b1-f66a-5f1d-ad45-2673438230d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-47498" :question/problem "A car travels on a straight road in such a way that its position, in meters, after $t$ seconds is given by the function $f(t).$ The values of $f(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(t)$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $14$ | $15$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the velocity ${f}^{′}(t)$ at the point $t=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{f(t+h)-f(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=4$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{f(4+2)-f(4-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(6)-f(2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the car at the instant of time $t=4$ is $0.75\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078607 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "47fdd234-4281-5a38-aa51-22a8934d48a4" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3380260b-e523-5086-a894-4d8f8bf9fdd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507671} {:answer/id #uuid "3599af72-f95a-547c-ba9a-fa458f70f570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507675} {:answer/id #uuid "391dd3a9-0b1b-5cc6-a2f9-5c1ec302e259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507680} {:answer/id #uuid "9a7f9747-962b-5ef8-ae18-b6975de0ec0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507813} {:answer/id #uuid "f9905493-fe7b-54f0-8777-6376ee8c61c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507936}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9905493-fe7b-54f0-8777-6376ee8c61c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507936} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1257117-ddc2-5b07-841b-2f9e8a671fda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "862b2bca-cb58-5918-b28a-220de43ef262" :question/math-academy-id "q-47533" :question/problem "![](images/52/52d37029cc93ea1e0be1c9a1488aa3275437c4be2b749ff09a497935de8399a4.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $g(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+2)-g(4-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(6)-g(2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078606 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6803a7be-e0e9-5f19-bd0b-711f49853170" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105028d2-d6dd-5dcf-a926-5082b7f0367c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1.7)≈7.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507620} {:answer/id #uuid "3b4bea6e-bb16-5316-9214-10da85ada450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1.7)≈5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507685} {:answer/id #uuid "3cdeb52d-d5c4-52b2-84f7-ac0b9a9f49e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1.7)≈6.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507690} {:answer/id #uuid "4dfca398-b647-5b5d-8ae1-37d9307ce4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1.7)≈1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507717} {:answer/id #uuid "ae998191-ec29-5aca-94bf-db5f5f3e0b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1.7)≈4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "105028d2-d6dd-5dcf-a926-5082b7f0367c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(1.7)≈7.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507620} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fe4a4bf-9911-5202-9b58-2e8068c15035" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61df167c-8856-5b89-8c68-3c6ad59fc5b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-4809" :question/problem "Given the following data for a function $f(x):$\n\n| **$x$** | $1.1$ | $1.3$ | $1.5$ | $1.7$ | $1.9$ | $2.1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $12$ | $15$ | $21$ | $23$ | $24$ | $25$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=1.7$ using a central difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=1.7.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1.7) & ≈\\frac{f(1.7+0.2)-f(1.7-0.2)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1.9)-f(1.5)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-21}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{0.4} \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332878 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078608 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24265d78-819c-5988-b582-ea8cc29f061c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330259} {:answer/id #uuid "46912e59-1bd4-5051-b1a0-dba014f012f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.05\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330586} {:answer/id #uuid "8c562598-41b8-5c48-964d-0505e00da5b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331196} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d384e4-4ea2-55f9-94d9-867acdced7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331406} {:answer/id #uuid "a793588b-2a9a-563b-a526-fe17cec1ff70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24265d78-819c-5988-b582-ea8cc29f061c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330259} :answer-field/id #uuid "31d4a9e5-c745-5774-b2c2-c53d83fc4b40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c6e93bc-4fb5-52a4-975a-8dfbc53642f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-51402" :question/problem "Sam wanted to estimate the rate of weight growth of his new puppy. He took note of its weight every week, for $7$ weeks. The results are shown in the table below, where $W(t)$ is the puppy's weight (measured in pounds) after $t$ weeks from birth.\n\n| **$t$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $W(t)$ | $9$ | $10.1$ | $11.3$ | $12.4$ | $13.5$ | $14.6$ | $15.8$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the puppy's rate of weight growth $12$ weeks after birth using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{W(t+h)-W(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=12$ and step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(0.2) & ≈\\frac{W(12+1)-W(12-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{W(13)-W(11)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14.6-12.4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.2}{2} \\\\  & =1.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the rate of weight growth at the instant of time $t=12$ is $1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078608 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ee0af75-bcb6-5b60-b0e8-3fd1b8dc76bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-50{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507634} {:answer/id #uuid "2b483a84-5c97-56c1-906f-fbb9b1f1e3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-30{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507650} {:answer/id #uuid "65de6908-4c51-5436-83fd-aa3e0f24419f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-20{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507747} {:answer/id #uuid "738573b4-cd3c-5ee2-b300-6d4a28ee74b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-45{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507768} {:answer/id #uuid "f5023fca-8043-5cc4-96cc-7e4e7ac32a5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-15{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b483a84-5c97-56c1-906f-fbb9b1f1e3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-30{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507650} :answer-field/id #uuid "a16e3a72-88b6-545d-81dc-981c40d41aa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2ff1bdc-524d-5a25-83f2-62b0e84aa209" :question/math-academy-id "q-51404" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4ede7ee4b2f41d19ba36d8e1cb28e9ab480a54c83310686baa35e7d08a7e7fd4.png)\n\nA liquid is heated to ${150}^{∘}\\text{C}$ and then left to cool. The temperature of the liquid after $t$ hours is given by $T(t).$  The graph of $T(t)$ is shown above.\n\nApproximate the rate of change of temperature when $t=2$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{T}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{T(t+h)-T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=2$ and step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{T(2+1)-T(2-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(3)-T(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{60-120}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-60}{2} \\\\  & =-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of temperature at the instant of time $t=2$ is $-30{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078608 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9fa7f8-708a-5006-9b9b-ea2c0334cb2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative Given a Graph Using a Central Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a00187-cbc3-5317-b9e6-87f2abfe2bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330126} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9de2d0-f9be-5cb4-96dd-ac8265f872ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330359} {:answer/id #uuid "8be85c09-ef47-5f5f-a842-3cc277864a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331191} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd28547-b0d9-5df0-a990-031060b1d5ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331628} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe7849e-d032-5002-9336-c465f7fd494c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e9de2d0-f9be-5cb4-96dd-ac8265f872ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330359} :answer-field/id #uuid "3286ba04-ae3e-5cab-8f4c-55cb8cefd221" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14f1836e-031c-5d94-96ad-23aaab157b74" :question/math-academy-id "q-51405" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1e11260301be8c0bb19a9fd47ffbbf71cc5fa4d94dbeae57af934b76fb17f0e1.png)\n\nA particle has a speed of $v(t)$ meters per second after $t$ seconds. The graph of $v(t)$ is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of speed when $t=3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{v}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{v(t+h)-g(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=2$ and step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{v(3+1)-v(3-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{v(4)-v(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of speed at the instant of time $t=2$ is approximately $1\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}.$"}]}
